From: Henk Wiedig <hwiedig@googlemail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: artosyn: SC231AI, the P1's second camera

BetaFPV fits either an NT99235 or a SmartSens SC231AI to the P1 air unit,
on the same connector, power and reset lines and master clock (the stock
sensor_board_cfg.cjson lists both). This adds the SC231AI and makes the
capture chain take its RAW10 frames.

- sc231ai: a V4L2 subdev for the vendor's linear 1080p60 two-lane RAW10
  mode (742.5 Mbps a lane, 24 MHz MCLK), exposure and gain as writable
  module parameters on the NT99235's gain code scale, mirror/flip as a
  live parameter (default off, as the vendor; the ISP's Bayer phase stays
  in all four orientations, so this is where a picture is turned), and the
  sensor's test pattern
  (0x4501 bit 3, a ramp with all four Bayer channels equal) as a
  parameter. The sensor sends exactly
  1920x1080; a bordered 1924-pixel RAW10 line would be 2405 bytes and
  breaks the two-lane CSI-2 packing with CRC errors.
- One DT node for either sensor: both compatibles, both addresses by
  reg-names. Each driver reads the chip ID at probe and returns -ENODEV
  when its sensor is absent (the NT99235 now probes to stage 3 by
  default), so the fitted one binds.
- ar-csi2, ar-vif: the CSI-2 data type follows the sensor's bus format;
  RAW10 gets its own IPI timing, no border in the VIF margin, and the line
  blanking follows the arriving width (the NT99235's 0x282 unchanged).
- ar-isp: ar_isp_pipeline_start takes the input format. The SC231AI needs
  the borderless input mode, its Bayer order and the second DRC length;
  the black level enable follows the tuning file (no change for the
  NT99235, whose tuning has it clear). White balance gains are new module
  parameters plus a white_balance debugfs file, unset by default so the
  NT99235 keeps its current state. A tuning= parameter on ar-isp and
  ar-cvisp picks the bound sensor's tuning file.
- ar-vif: stop no longer clears the AXI interface's enable and run bits,
  and the global init keeps them. Clearing them wedges the ISP's pixel
  output until the SoC is reset: every frame then aborts with NR3D AXI
  and DMA errors. A boot-time start that fails (e.g. the image's camera
  start with the other sensor fitted) is enough to wedge it.

The RAW10 input mode, Bayer order, DRC lengths, IPI timing and the AXI
behaviour were found by the fpvOS project (github.com/gehee/fpvOS), whose
SC231AI support runs on the same ml-kernel; reimplemented here from those
register facts. Tested on a P1 with an SC231AI (RAM boot): ISP statistics
826 zones, no ISP error interrupts, AE live, stream stop/restart and a
module reload without the wedge.

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/artosyn/proxima-9311-air.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/artosyn/proxima-9311-air.dts
index 4ef1a4a..a3a38ae 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/artosyn/proxima-9311-air.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/artosyn/proxima-9311-air.dts
@@ -331,10 +331,18 @@
 			 * Two lanes: the four sensor modes split into 4-lane (720p90, 1080p60) and
 			 * 2-lane (540p120, 1080p60-2lane) variants selected by sensor register
 			 * 0x0114, and the unit was captured running the 2-lane 1080p60 mode.
-			 * Whether the board routes more than two lanes is unresolved. */
+			 * Whether the board routes more than two lanes is unresolved.
+			 *
+			 * Other P1 units carry a SmartSens SC231AI instead (I2C 0x30, RAW10,
+			 * two lanes) on the same connector, lines and clock; the stock
+			 * sensor_board_cfg.cjson lists both. One node serves either: each
+			 * driver reads the chip ID at probe and steps aside with -ENODEV
+			 * when its sensor is not fitted, and the SC231AI driver claims its
+			 * own address through reg-names. */
 			nt99235: camera-sensor@1a {
-				compatible = "novatek,nt99235";
-				reg = <0x1a>;
+				compatible = "novatek,nt99235", "smartsens,sc231ai";
+				reg = <0x1a>, <0x30>;
+				reg-names = "nt99235", "sc231ai";
 				reset-gpios = <&gpio 107 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 				enable-gpios = <&gpio 104 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 				clocks = <&pixclk 35>;		/* cgu_sensor_mclk0 */
diff --git a/drivers/media/artosyn/Kconfig b/drivers/media/artosyn/Kconfig
index 7ee843e..086c636 100644
--- a/drivers/media/artosyn/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/media/artosyn/Kconfig
@@ -13,6 +13,19 @@ config VIDEO_ARTOSYN_NT99235
 	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module will be
 	  called nt99235.
 
+config VIDEO_ARTOSYN_SC231AI
+	tristate "SmartSens SC231AI sensor support"
+	depends on OF && I2C && VIDEO_DEV
+	select MEDIA_CONTROLLER
+	select VIDEO_V4L2_SUBDEV_API
+	select V4L2_FWNODE
+	help
+	  Subdev driver for the SmartSens SC231AI MIPI CSI-2 image sensor,
+	  the second camera BetaFPV fits to the P1 air unit.
+
+	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module will be
+	  called sc231ai.
+
 config VIDEO_ARTOSYN_CSI2
 	tristate "Artosyn MIPI CSI-2 receiver"
 	depends on OF && VIDEO_DEV
diff --git a/drivers/media/artosyn/Makefile b/drivers/media/artosyn/Makefile
